outputs.L1:
An optoelectronic semiconductor component is disclosed, comprising:

- a semiconductor body (1) including a semiconductor layer sequence (2) with a p-type semiconductor region (3), an n-type semiconductor region (5), and an active layer (4) disposed between the p-type semiconductor region (3) and the n-type semiconductor region (5);
- a support (10) comprising a plastic material and including a first via (11) and a second via (12);
- a p-contact layer (7) and an n-contact layer (8), at least portions of which are disposed between the support (10) and the semiconductor body (1), wherein the p-contact layer (7) connects the first via (11) to the p-type semiconductor region (3), and the n-contact layer (8, 8A) connects the second via (12) to the n-type semiconductor region (5); and
- an ESD protection element (15) disposed between the support (10) and the semiconductor body (1), wherein the ESD protection element (15) is electrically conductively connected to the first via (11) and the second via (12), and wherein the forward direction of the ESD protection element (15) is antiparallel to the forward direction of the semiconductor layer sequence (2).

counterfactuals.output:
1. **An optoelectronic semiconductor component**, comprising:  

   a semiconductor layer sequence including a p-type semiconductor region, an n-type semiconductor region, and an active layer arranged between the p-type semiconductor region and the n-type semiconductor region and configured to generate or detect electromagnetic radiation;  

   a plastic support having a first via and a second via extending through the plastic support;  

   a first contact layer electrically coupling the p-type semiconductor region to an electrically conductive material disposed in the first via;  

   a second contact layer electrically coupling the n-type semiconductor region to an electrically conductive material disposed in the second via; and  

   an electrostatic-discharge protection element integrated into the optoelectronic semiconductor component and electrically connected between the first contact layer and the second contact layer in anti-parallel with a p-n junction formed by the p-type semiconductor region, the active layer, and the n-type semiconductor region.

1. An optoelectronic apparatus comprising:  

   a plastic support comprising a first via and a second via;  

   an optoelectronic semiconductor chip mounted on the plastic support and comprising a p-type semiconductor region and an n-type semiconductor region;  

   a p-contact layer electrically coupling the p-type semiconductor region to the first via;  

   an n-contact layer electrically coupling the n-type semiconductor region to the second via; and  

   an electrostatic-discharge diode integrated between the optoelectronic semiconductor chip and the plastic support and electrically connected between the first via and the second via in anti-parallel with the optoelectronic semiconductor chip.
